block head
    title Carotenosis - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Carotenosis
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carotenosis") Wikipedia]:
    blockquote Carotenosis is a benign and reversible medical condition where an excess of dietary carotenoids results in orange discoloration of the outermost skin layer. The discoloration is most easily observed in light-skinned people and may be mistaken for jaundice.

